# Working on this project

This project was generated with Nutin {{version}}.

## Architecture

```
src/
  app/            application code (components, views, services)
  core/           Nutin framework internals — see "Nutin" section before editing
  styles/         project-level Sass
config/           i18n (languages.json) and SEO configuration
tools/            builder, dev server, generator, testin-nutin runner, docker (optional)
nutin.config.js   build/feature config — see below
.nutin-meta.json  Nutin version, package manager, enabled features (source of truth for what's installed)
```

## Conventions

- Favor small, composable components.
- One `View` = one route.
- Import everything from barrel files (`core/index.js`, `components/index.js`, `views/index.js`, `services/index.js`) — do not deep-import.

## Commands

- Serve: `{{packageManager}} run serve` (build + serve), `{{packageManager}} run serve:only` (no rebuild), `{{packageManager}} run dev` (watch mode).
- Build: `{{packageManager}} run build` (dev) or `{{packageManager}} run build:prod` (production).
- Generate: `{{packageManager}} run generate ELEMENT ELEMENT_NAME` (`ELEMENT` = `component`/`view`/`service`, supports nested paths, updates the nearest `index.ts` barrel).
- Test: `{{packageManager}} run testin-nutin` (build + run), `{{packageManager}} run testin-nutin:only` (no rebuild), `{{packageManager}} run testin-nutin:watch`.

## Base classes

```
Service<T>          — app-wide singleton (router, event bus, i18n, http client, pipe registry, app-specific services)
BaseComponent<T>     — render/destroy engine, data-* parsing, children
├── Component        — reusable, non-routed UI; config/props + data-bind
└── View              — one per route; mounted/unmounted by the Router
```

- `render()`: `onBeforeRender()` → sanitize + set `innerHTML` → mount children (`data-component`/`data-catalog`) → parse `data-i18n`/`data-pipe` → bind `data-event` listeners → `onAfterRender()`. Runs in full on every `render()` call — no virtual DOM/diffing.
- `destroy()`: unbinds events, unsubscribes bus listeners, destroys children, removes the element.
- `Service`: direct `new` throws — always use `MyService.getInstance()` (or the exported const). Auto-binds all methods to the instance. `registerCleanup(fn)` for teardown; `Service.destroyAll()` runs on `beforeunload`.
- Overridable hooks (all no-op by default): `onBeforeRender`, `onAfterRender`, `onBeforeDestroy`, `onAfterDestroy`, `generateTemplate()`, `registerChildren()`. `View` adds router-only `onEnter()`/`onExit()`.

## Children components

- Override `registerChildren(): ComponentConfig[]` to declare children — matched against `[data-component="selector"]` elements in the rendered template. ComponentConfig: `{ selector: 'my-selector', factory: (el) => new MyComponent(el, {...} )}`.
- For repeated lists, use the inherited `createCatalogComponents({ items, elementName, selector, component })` inside `registerChildren()` instead of hand-writing one entry per item — targets `[data-catalog="selector"]`.

## `data-*` attributes

| Attribute | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `data-event="event:handler[:args]"` | Declarative event binding, see below. |
| `data-i18n="key"` | Sets translated text/placeholder via `I18nService`. |
| `data-pipe="name[:args]\|name2..."` | Pipes value/text through registered pipes, chainable with `\|`. |
| `data-pipe-source="..."` | Overrides the raw value fed into `data-pipe`. |
| `data-optional` | Removes the element post-render if it ends up empty (tag-specific check: `src`/`value`/`textContent`). |
| `data-component="selector"` | Child component mount point, from `registerChildren()`. |
| `data-catalog="selector"` | Repeated-children mount point, from `createCatalogComponents()`. |
| `data-bind="propKey"` | `Component`-only two-way field binding; read back with `getValues()`. |

## DOM events binding

Handlers are (re-)bound on every `render()`, not at build time. Always use private methods prefixed with underscore:

```html
<div data-event="event:_myFunction:@value,@id">
```
```ts
private _myFunction(value: string, id: string) { doStuff() }
```

Tokens: `@value`, `@id`, `@class`, `@textContent`, `@event`, `@target`, `@attr:name`, `@dataset:key`, plus string/number literals.

## Core services

- `AppEventBus` — `subscribe`/`once`/`emit`/`off`. Inside a component, prefer `this.listen(event, cb)` (auto-unsubscribes on `destroy()`) or `this.listenToRenderEvents([event1, event2, ...])` (re-runs `this.render()` whenever any of the given events fire) over calling the bus directly. Typed facades — each `on*` subscriber returns a closure you call directly to unsubscribe (`const off = Navigation.onNavigate(cb); ...; off();`), no need to keep the original callback reference around for `off()`:
  - `Navigation` — `navigateTo(path)`/`onNavigate`, `reload()`/`onReload`.
  - `Lifecycle` — `viewMount(viewName)`/`onViewMount`, `viewUnmount(viewName)`/`onViewUnmount`, plus generic `beforeRender`/`afterRender`/`beforeDestroy`/`afterDestroy`.
- `AppRouter(routes)` — call once in `main.ts`; routes support `:param`/`:param?` and per-route guards.
- `registerGlobals({ before?, after? })` — each entry is `{ component, id }` (a bare class, constructed internally); mounts them outside `<main id="app">` (`before`/`after` control placement relative to it), stamping each root element with `id`. `hideGlobals(ids)`/`revealGlobals(ids)` (same module) toggle visibility by those ids from any component or view. Call once in `main.ts`.
- `AppHttpClient` — `get/post/put/patch/delete<T>(endpoint, data?, config?)`; non-OK responses throw `HttpError`.
- `I18nService` — `translate(key, fallback?)`, `setCurrentLanguage(lang)`; language list comes from `config/languages.json`.
- `AppPipeRegistry` — `register(name, fn)` / `apply(name, value, args)`; backs `data-pipe`.

## Styling

- Sass is the primary styling system; Tailwind is optional (`nutin.config.js`'s `tailwind` flag).
- Naming convention: `.my-element__my-class`.

## Pipes

```
// currency
AppPipeRegistry.register('currency');
    
// date
AppPipeRegistry.register('date');

// number (toFixed)
AppPipeRegistry.register('number');

// string pipes
AppPipeRegistry.register('uppercase');
AppPipeRegistry.register('lowercase');    
AppPipeRegistry.register('capitalize');
AppPipeRegistry.register('capitalizeAll');
AppPipeRegistry.register('truncate');
    
// utility pipes
AppPipeRegistry.register('default');
AppPipeRegistry.register('json');
```

## Configuration

### `nutin.config.js`

Central options/tools config (see the inline comments for details):
- `i18n`, `tailwind`, `generateSEO`, `dockerPorts` — top-level feature toggles (`dockerPorts` only applies once the docker feature is added).
- `generator.{generateStylesheet, generateLocales, generateTest}` — what the generator scaffolds alongside new elements.
- `builder.{sass.paths, esbuild}` — build pipeline behavior.
- `testinNutin.{includeFramework, includeTools, includeApp, verbose, jsdomOptions}` — test discovery/environment.

### `config/seo.json`

Consumed by builder (production only) to generate static HTML per route. Unused if `nutin.config.js -> generateSEO` is disabled.

### `config/languages.json`

Consumed by i18nService and builder. Unused if i18n is disabled.

## Security

`SecurityHelper.sanitizeTemplate()` runs on every `render()` before `innerHTML` is set — `trustLevel` (`'strict' | 'normal' | 'trusted'`, default `'normal'`) controls how much is stripped (`<script>`/inline handlers always; `<iframe>`/`javascript:`/`data:` under `strict` only). Use `SecurityHelper.escapeHtml()` when manually interpolating strings into templates.

## Testing (testin-nutin)

Nutin's own hand-built test runner + jsdom - not Jest. `describe`/`it` only (**no `test()` alias**), `beforeAll`/`beforeEach`/`afterEach`/`afterAll` (one of each per suite, no stacking - inside `describe` statement, not top-level). All globals — no imports needed in test files.

- Matchers: `toBe`, `toEqual`, `toContain`, `toBeTruthy`/`toBeFalsy`, `toBeDefined`/`toBeUndefined`, `toBeInstanceOf`, `toHaveBeenCalled`/`toHaveBeenCalledWith`, `toBeLessThan`/`toBeGreaterThan`, `toThrow` — each has a `.not` counterpart.
- `spyOn(obj, 'method')` returns `.calls`/`.callCount`/`.lastCall`, `.andCallFake(fn)`/`.andReturn(v)`, `.restore()` — unlike mocks, calls pass through by default.
- `tools/testin-nutin/mocks/` has ready-made `MockEventBus`/`MockHttpClient`/`MockI18n`/`MockRouter` for constructor injection.
- `useFakeTimers()`/`useRealTimers()`/`advanceTimersByTime(ms)`/`runAllTimers()` for time-dependent code.
- Test discovery/scope controlled by `nutin.config.js`'s `testinNutin.includeApp`/`includeFramework`.

## Nutin

Nutin provides the project tooling, build pipeline and generated structure. Its source code lives in `src/core/`.

Tests are an important source of documentation. They describe expected behavior and should be consulted before modifying existing functionality.
Before changing existing functionality, inspect the corresponding tests.
When adding behavior, add or update tests.

When modifying Nutin `core/` files:

1. Explore the alternatives: is modifying Nutin core files the best approach long-term? Always ask for validation.
2. Check the corresponding Nutin documentation and tests.
3. Preserve existing conventions.
4. Inspect existing implementations before creating new abstractions.
5. Reuse existing utilities/helpers where appropriate.
6. Do not rewrite generated configuration unnecessarily.
7. Keep changes focused on the requested feature.
8. Run tests.

